- Major improvements

1. Beat-detection plugins

Still the most laborious and error-prone of the process.
Many tracks have click-track, very even and clean timing.
Others have messy timing.
Tempo and beat detection are not just onset, but inertia.
Inserting all beats by hand, even with extrapolation, smoothing, and beat-detection assist is still laborious.

2. Musical score: RiffText

Need a way to store riffs, musical passages, chord voices, fingers, tab.
Want to go from simple chords to riffs, motifs, and solos.
Most tracks I care about already have Guitar pros.
Should be able to load / align Guitar Pro tabs.
Include audio and video cues for karaoke to nail tricky passages.

3. Transcription: use plugins

Plugins should be able to automatically transcribe drums, bass, guitar, voice.

4. Lyrics / Voice

Plugins can go search the internet for vocals, align vocal lines / passages, maybe even transcribe.
It'd be great to have one tool that marks vocal lines and another tool that matches found / pasted lyrics.
Transcribe the melody of vocal passage, both lead, harmonies, backing, interjections, etc.
Increase precision with beat-precise lyric alignment.

5. Stem separation

Make it possible to practice against a track with a stem removed or "stubbed"--where the melody or rhythm is replaced with clicks, synth'd notes, or other cues.


Fixes:
- Linux audio playback / generation never worked.

Stretch:
- Try web/wasm build

- Analyzer plugins / audio analysis
  - Allow (out-of-process) plugins to analyze raw audio samples and return results
  - Spectral fingerprint analysis
    - select kick drum / snare, find others
  - Stem extraction
  - Lyric alignment
  - Transcription
- Load dialog should allow up and down arrows
- section duplicate tool:
  - duplicates the beat pattern and measures of a given section (e.g. verse)
  - the new pasted section can be dragged on the timeline,
  - but analysis tools help match its structure to the underlying audio (i.e. find and fix to the right beats)
  - bonus: automatically find verse 2 from verse 1.
- better bulk insertion
  - global BPM inference range setting (e.g. 50 to 180bpm)
  - mark beginning and end of section, offer subdivision choice 2=100bpm,3,4=200bpm,5
  - reinterpolate beats between (delete and reinsert)
  - insert measure(s) 4,8,12 beats
- Chord progressions per section
  - Simple chord change cue?
  - DONE: misc annotations select as a group (shift+click, shift+drag) and
    cut/copy/paste with Ctrl+X/C/V; paste anchors the group at the playhead
    (snapped to the nearest beat) and carries beat offsets, not seconds, so a
    verse copied onto a drifting live take still lands on its beats
  - DONE: lyric and misc blocks drag in time (edges still resize); a misc drag
    moves the whole selected group.  Lyric body drag had never worked -- its
    arming condition compared the selection to the entry it had just selected
  - next: the same for whole sections, and "chords from the first verse" as a
    reference rather than a copy
- Lyric mode: larger, higher resolution font
  - button to copy previous or other lyric
- Global audit of all do/undo/redo history
  - DONE: snapshots now cover beats/lyrics/sections/misc per-layer, no-op edits
    no longer push entries, and the stack is cleared when a track or beatmap is
    loaded (it used to be restorable onto the wrong track)
  - remaining: inline text edits (lyric / misc / section labels) are not
    undoable; there is still no redo

- Settings dialog for all panels.
- Beat-precise lyrics. In the lyric editing timeline pane, there is a way to line up beats with individual words and syllables.
